_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":572781997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1NzI3ODE5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:audio","name":"topic:audio","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-08-07T13:24:14Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T14:57:58Z","closed_at":"2025-08-07T14:55:08Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109393","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109393.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109393.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This adds a very cheap to process bitcrusher effect that just lowers the sample rate of the bus.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Why?\r\n\r\nMany games use this effect, either to emulate a \"retro\" feeling or to have some \"disturbing/horror\" vibe.\r\n\r\n### Potential enhancements\r\n\r\nThe max sample rate in the editor is set to 44100Hz, but the user's audioserver sample rate might be different (e.g: 48000Hz). Is there a proper way to change this?\r\n\r\n### Showcase\r\n\r\nmusic is \"Yoni Mayraz - Dybbuk Tse!\"\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae9b2e44-b020-45a5-87b8-eebdb4620aa0\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a47daee0-2103-4bfd-b51b-8bcbb6d5870e\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nP.S:  I used the \"amplifier\" effect code as a template for making this one, if things aren't necessary and can be removed, I might have missed some of them.\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/5810*","closed_by":{"login":"ObaniGemini","id":11649956,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjQ5OTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11649956?v=4","gravatar_id":